 "titulo": "The radio said my name 😰 Part 2 #horror #shorts",
 "capa": "TURN OFF THE LIGHT",
 "descripcion": "S.O.S., blinking at the lighthouse window. The coast guard said no boat was out. Then the radio used Eli's name.\n\n> Part 3: {when_next}.\nWhat would you do?\n\nNarrated fiction. New part every day.\n#horror #horrorstories #scarystories #survival #creepypasta",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "S, O, S. Blinking right at my window.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Morse code. Slow, careful, like someone learned it a very long time ago.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Every rule said answer a mayday. Except this one.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "I took my hand off the microphone, and I waited.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "So I called the coast guard on the landline.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The officer listened, then went quiet for a second.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "They said no boat was out tonight. Not one.",
   "pausa": 0.8
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then he asked: did you answer it? I said no. He said: good. Don't.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then the radio spoke again, and it said my name.",
   "pausa": 0.8
  },
  {
   "texto": "Nobody out there should know my name. Nobody.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Eli, we see your light. Turn it off, so we can come in.",
   "pausa": 0.9
  },
  {
   "texto": "The rules never said why the light must keep turning.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "A lighthouse keeps ships away from the rocks.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Tonight I understood. It kept something else away too.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Whatever was out there wanted to come closer.",
   "pausa": 0.9
  },
  {
   "texto": "Part three, {when_next}.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
